>ISHIKAWA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIKUCHI KAZUTSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATOH YOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI YOSHITAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YACHI MASANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIKUCHI, KAZUTSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATOH, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>Takahashi, Yoshitaka</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YACHI, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A tuning fork type vibrational gyroscope, wherein a tuning fork type oscillator having two arms and a base is supported on a supporting substrate installed on a stem, and an oscillation limiting member comprising an annular rubber elastic body is installed so that it surrounds the base with its one face fixed to the stem, whereby though, when a vibration or impact is given externally, the tuning fork type oscillator is oscillated according to the vibration or impact, the amplitude of the tuning fork type oscillator is limited by the presence of an oscillating limiting member so as to prevent the tuning fork type oscillator from impacting against surrounding members such as the stem, and a gyro characteristic is not impaired and also there is no possibility that a gyro function is lost due to stop of driving vibration.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un gyroscope vibratoire du type à diapason dans lequel un oscillateur du type à diapason présentant deux bras et une base est porté sur un substrat de support installé sur une tige, et un élément limitant les oscillations comprenant un corps annulaire en caoutchouc élastique est installé de manière à entourer la base avec sa face fixée à la tige de manière que, bien que lorsqu'une vibration ou un impact est donné de l'extérieur, l'oscillateur du type à diapason oscille selon la vibration ou l'impact, l'amplitude de l'oscillateur du type à diapason est limitée par la présence d'un élément limitant l'oscillation afin d'empêcher que l'oscillateur du type à diapason ne heurte des éléments environnants tels que la tige, et qu'une caractéristique du gyroscope ne soit détériorée, de même il n'existe aucune possibilité qu'une fonction du gyroscope ne soit perdue du fait d'un arrêt des vibrations de commande.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>